<!--Post: 2010--><!--Time: 1103244319-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2010"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jim44095<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jim44095<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 4:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How did he know that the Otero daughter would be home from school that day?Did he see the father drop off the other 2 or did he take the call from the mother calling them off?This has always bothered me,I think the daughter was the target in the first place.Any insight you can give Mike would be appreciated.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2010-->
<!--Post: 2011--><!--Time: 1103244500-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2011"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 4:48 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Please reserve comments in this thread to Kelleher&#39;s profile.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2011-->
<!--Post: 2023--><!--Time: 1103253807-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2023"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 7:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Jim: <BR> <BR>It&#39;s impossible to say. However, it is very likely that BTK had spent some time observing the family before the attack. In fact, he may have known their movements and habits well. It&#39;s not unusual for a serial killer to strike close to home at the early stages of his career. In fact, it&#39;s not all that unusual for the killer to know his first victim&#40;s&#41; in some way. If I were just walking into the case, I would want to know as much as possible about the Otero attack since it would likely yield the best profile of the killer. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2023-->
<!--Post: 2028--><!--Time: 1103256969-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2028"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 8:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, <BR>In regards to your comment above &#34;I would want to know as much as possible about the Otero attack.&#34; <BR> <BR>What&#39;s your take on Charlie Otero&#39;s statements about his fathers strange behavior for &#34;days&#34; leading up to the day of the crime? <BR> <BR>It would seem to me that the father is the key to focus on if he was &#34;expecting&#34; something he feared that much.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2028-->
<!--Post: 2041--><!--Time: 1103262830-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2041"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 16, 2004 - 9:53 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q: <BR> <BR>Hard to say. It could be memory-filling, which is common after a violent incident. It&#39;s the type of behavior that represents a &#34;searching&#34; or &#34;rationale&#34; for why the incident happened. In other words, looking for reason where there is no reason. Of course, it could also be true, in which case Otero was fearful for some reason, which could also make sense. With the lack of any other pertinent information, I would tend to go with memory filling as the safest course. We all do it and it&#39;s a very understandable reaction to that kind of trauma. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2041-->
<!--Post: 2154--><!--Time: 1103340795-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2154"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 7:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike, I&#39;m not sure I buy into the memory filling theory. <BR> <BR>The things Charlie Otero speaks of are quite specific, such as, his father having him look out the window for a company vehicle &#40;which is interesting that he would have his son do it and the putting them all in the closet. <BR> <BR>On the other hand the idea that his Dad did not protect him &#40;sending him to look&#41; and also did &#40;hiding them&#41; does fill the need for some resolution, albeit temporary in all likely hood, of the anger he must have had/has? <BR> <BR>Do you agree? <BR> <BR>Charlie Otero claims to not have been interviewed since the 70&#39;s if I remember. How thorough is that? The terror this guy has lived with surely must feed BTKs ego. The Anna why letter and the general aspect of the fear or &#34;terrorism&#34; is certainly a source for ego gratification for this Murderer. Do you see these aspects as seperate games/interests for him or all part of one big sick twisted plan? <BR> <BR>Do you know what happend to Shirley Vians Kids?  <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2154-->
<!--Post: 2166--><!--Time: 1103344814-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2166"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 17, 2004 - 8:40 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Regarding Charlie Otero and &#39;memory filling&#39; I prefer to call it memory embellishment.  It may be that his memory for his dad being worried is right on the money.  But it is possible, as Mr. Kelleher suggests, that some event was built up in his mind in an effort to &#39;make sense&#39; of such a horrible and on the surface, senseless crime.  Perhaps Mr. Otero asked him to check if an official vehicle was outside because he suspected a salesman or panhandler at the door, and did not want to answer in that case.  Such an innocent event could have become suspicious in young Charlie&#39;s mind after the murders, which would be quite understandable. <BR>I am also cruious as to if Mr. Kellher has had to opportunity to visit the crime scenes?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2166-->
<!--Post: 2704--><!--Time: 1103962971-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2704"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 12:22 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dr. Kelleher, <BR> <BR>I have been reading your profile on Zodiac that was posted on a diffrent website. I found it to  <BR>be very intresting and informitive. It is much more in depth then your BTK profile and while  <BR>I assume you have a great more knowledge on that case then BTK, I found it intresting how diffrent they are from one another. I say this, because I find there motivations and killing methods very similar. I was wondering if you could post a kind of comparing and contrasting of the two cases. Also, if there was anything new you would add to your BTK profile since so much more info has been released and so much has happened in regard to the case, with the new communications.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2704-->
<!--Post: 2768--><!--Time: 1104095069-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2768"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, December 26, 2004 - 1:04 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Scbenson: <BR> <BR>There was a great deal of information available about Zodiac, which made the job a bit easier. I do have much more to say on BTK but not right now. I need to do more research and a good deal more thinking about him. Plus, I&#39;m just starting off on a new book, so my time is limited. I have a real fascination with BTK and I do see a good deal of similarities between the two killers. However, it just has to wait, for now. Sorry. When I have the time and inclination, I&#39;ll send something Tom&#39;s way and he can decide what to do with it. <BR> <BR>Mike <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2768-->
<!--Post: 2797--><!--Time: 1104150546-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2797"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 4:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thank you for the quick respone. I look forward to your new book. It should be very intresting. Please keep us posted with its progress. For now I&#39;ll have to busy myself with reading &#34;This Is the Zodiac Speaking&#34; Thanks again and Happy Holidays to you. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2797-->
<!--Post: 3013--><!--Time: 1104371506-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3013"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 5:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike_kelleher: <BR>I&#39;m with Q on this one.  I am amazed at the amount of data that is being discarded as wrong without any objective evidence that it is.  I agree with Q in the sense that IF Charlie Otero is accurately reporting an accurate memory THEN it was not a random killing. <BR> <BR>I am well aware of the &#34;memory filling&#34; you refer to, but it usually occurs in traumatic amnesia victims or people who have dissasociative reactions.  It can happen in this kind of event, BUT IS THERE ANY EVIDENCE THAT IT DID?. Has anyone interviewed the other surviving sibling? <BR> <BR>How about reworking your profile as a &#34;decision tree&#34; with contravening assumptions plugged in as an alternative.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3013-->
<!--Post: 3177--><!--Time: 1104549565-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3177"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 7:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Memory filling is common to all of us to a greater or lesser degree, and as a function of time. It is a natural and expected process. A decision tree is probably the poorest way to profile an individual as it allows for only binary considerations and can easily lead the user of the profile in a completely wrong direction. Since profiling is rarely as accurate as it should be, the profiler must be extremely careful to not put the user of the profile into the position of choosing from two, equally incorrect possibilities. It&#39;s always  best to work with probabilities and refine them as more data is gathered. It&#39;s always unwise to think there is some kind of formula or fixed pattern to human behavior.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3177-->
<!--Post: 3178--><!--Time: 1104551898-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3178"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 7:58 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Interesting side note:  <BR> <BR>In the Possible Victims thread/Carol Mould: There are some links suggesting that her husband is the Doctor &#40;Dr. Douglas E. Mould&#41; that many links of his writings and criminal expert opinions as well as political opinion are provided. <BR> <BR>One of these is a conference he spoke at:  <BR> <BR>FMS  FOUNDATION   and   JOHNS  HOPKINS  MEDICAL  INSTITUTIONS <BR>present <BR> <BR>M E M O R Y   A N D    R E A L I T Y:   <BR>R E C O N C I L I A T I O N <BR> <BR>Scientific, Clinical and Legal Issues of <BR> <BR>False Memory Syndrome <BR> <BR>December 9 - 11, 1994 <BR>Stouffer Harborplace Hotel, Baltimore, Maryland <BR> <BR>&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42;&#42; <BR> <BR>Is memory filling and false memory syndrome considered to be the same Mike? <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR>Also one other erie thing that stood out in those links: Dr. Mould in writing about Womens violence against men: <BR> <BR>This is not a new issue for me &#40;Mould, 1984a, 1986, 1987, 1990a, 1990b&#41;. In 1984 the local United Way ran an ad showing a woman in sunglasses with an obviously bruised cheek. The headline read &#34;Her Mr. Right had a powerful left...&#34; <BR> <BR>Julie Otero is pictured wearing sunglasses and her cheek bone was broken but most often discribed as being bruised.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3178-->
<!--Post: 3179--><!--Time: 1104552069-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3179"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 31, 2004 - 8:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Although hardly the expert Mike is I have to agree with him completly. Mr. Otero&#39;s recollections of that day cannot be complete. The stress of finding the horror that had befallen his <BR>family and at such a young age would most certainly lead to alterations in reality. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3179-->
<!--Post: 3194--><!--Time: 1104603665-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3194"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 10:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sure but he isn&#39;t saying what color of socks his dad was wearing a week before he was murdered he is saying that his Dad made them all hide and other very specific actions.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3194-->
<!--Post: 3198--><!--Time: 1104606804-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3198"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, January 01, 2005 - 11:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Sounds to me alot like the drills we had to run while I was in elementary school during that same period. In case of nuclear war, if you can believe it they used to make us hide under our desks. Mr Otero was a military man and during this time period alot of military parents made their children do drills at home during this height of the cold war.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
