<!--Post: 3246--><!--Time: 1104668932-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3246"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 4:28 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is a link to the woman who states that she was a friend of Josephine Otero, posting on AMW. <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages?msg=489.28" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/foxamw/messages?msg=489 .28</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3246-->
<!--Post: 3255--><!--Time: 1104695396-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3255"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cyndi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cyndi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 11:49 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->WhoisBTK, I would like to address #3 of your proposed scenario.  If the two &#34;Osborne&#34; children could possibly identify BTK then why would he not wait and kill the remaining children when they arrived home from school?  If &#34;he&#34; possibly lived nearby or visited infrequently couldn&#39;t the other children identify him also?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3255-->
<!--Post: 3261--><!--Time: 1104703296-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3261"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 2:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q: <BR>Yes, tornado drill makes more sense for that part of the country AND that particular time. I found a web site listing the tornado history of KS and there were apparently 2 tornadoes hitting Sedgwick County in October &#39;73.  One of these injured 15 people, less than three months prior to the murders.  A key thing we&#39;re told when tornadoes approach - get into a closet in the middle of the house.  Perhaps the Otero parents had drills and Charlie&#39;s memory filling may have incorporated hiding in the closet in/around that time of his life. <BR> <BR>Back to the issue of the profile: <BR>I don&#39;t buy the notion of drug-dealing.  It seems to me the MO indicates a planned killing for the &#34;fun&#34; of it &#40;pardon me for saying it that way&#41;, whereas I suspect drug-related killing is more direct and quick &#40;walk in and shoot - not necessarily torture and ejaculate&#41;.  Mike, is this not true? <BR> <BR>Also, my guess has always been : a&#41; he may have had some killing experience prior to the Oteros &#40;maybe via war-related killing&#41;; b&#41; he knew at least one member of the Otero family and maybe some negative relationship made these people be selected as his &#34;debut&#34; into public killing; c&#41; now that he had these killings accomplished, the drive took hold and he went about planning the other killings, typically selecting young, lone, white thin light-colored hair victims.  If you&#39;ll notice the photos on this web site, Bright, Fox, and Wegerle have similar features.  I suspect Vian was a last minute plan; she didn&#39;t appear to be thin and particularly pretty.  Perhaps the photo he showed to the Vian child was of the INTENDED victim&#40;s&#41;, not Vian &#40;do we know?&#41; and when he failed to find them, he went with Vian instead. <BR> <BR>Mike: does this fit with your profile?  Do Sks follow a pattern like that: first major kill is of known victims, based on some personal issues, then a pattern of selecting unknown victims who share similar features? <BR> <BR>&#40;And, on this note....I&#39;ve not taken the time to read up on all of the possible victims. Do any of them fit the young, thin, blond pattern?&#41;<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3261-->
<!--Post: 3279--><!--Time: 1104727452-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3279"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 8:44 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->J: <BR> <BR>I do not see any evidence of a drug-related crime with any of BTK&#39;s activities. However, I do believe that BTK was familiar with the Otero family, or at least one member &#40;as you said&#41;. I would not put much stock in &#34;look alike&#34; victims in this case, simply because of the multiple murder aspect and the way the murders were carried out. It is possible but I wouldn&#39;t rate it highly likely. It is more likely that he knew each of the victims, although in a more passing way than the Oteros. I use the term &#34;knew&#34; here is a very loose sense, as in at least having seen the victims on several occasions before the attacks. I rather doubt that any of the murders were &#34;last minute.&#34; In fact, BTK was prepared, selected his victims, and planned accordingly. He was, to use an outdated way of thinking, an &#34;organized&#34; killer. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3279-->
<!--Post: 3281--><!--Time: 1104732990-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3281"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->J<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->J<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 02, 2005 - 10:16 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike: thanks so much for your quick response to my questions. <BR> <BR>I thought there were indeed cases where SKs choose look-alikes.  No?   <BR> <BR>The only mutliple event was the Oteros, right?  Wasn&#39;t Kevin Bright assumed to be unanticipated? <BR> <BR>By &#34;last minute&#34; on Vian, I meant to suggest a last minute &#42;switch&#42;.  IF the photo he showed to the kid was of someone he INTENDED to find &#40;not Vian&#41;, but the kid didn&#39;t give helpful info or BTK failed to locate the person....then maybe he switched to Vian instead &#40;since he was all prepared to kill that day&#41;.  This is just a thought and one that helps put Vian in a slightly separate category than Bright, Fox, Wegerle, and perhaps any additional possible victims yet to be linked.  Only BTK knows for sure, of course. <BR> <BR>I understand what you&#39;re saying about &#34;knowing&#34; the victims in a loose sense...perhaps via watching them from a distance, etc.  This still qualifies as &#34;unknown&#34; in my general definition &#40;i.e., BTK was unknown to them at least; no meaningful relationship existed between them.&#41; <BR> <BR>Thanks again for your response.  I admire your work and willingness to share your thoughts with us.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3281-->
<!--Post: 3287--><!--Time: 1104740126-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3287"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 12:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike_Kelleher <BR>J <BR>     I don&#39;t like drug dealing as the underlying issue either.  I think your idea of prior military related homicides is much better. But I think I think some issue/reason has to be present in some form because: <BR> <BR>&#42;IF&#42; Charlie is accurate about the fear, closet, etc. <BR> <BR>&#42;THEN&#42; there is a reason BTK threatens Mr. Osborne, and <BR> <BR>&#42;THEN&#42; there is a reason why Mr. Osborne won&#39;t ask police or adult friends for help.   <BR> <BR>We don&#39;t have to know what these reasons were for this hypothesis to function, but clearly this area of the hypothesis needs firming up. <BR> <BR>If anyone has suggestions about what these prior crime/event/reasons might be, please jump in. <BR> <BR> <BR>Cyndi: Those are good questions.  My thinking on your points, plus one more: <BR> <BR>Here’s One More:  We have assumed that BTK knew two of the five children remained at home, what if he didn’t.  He was surveilling the house most likely from a distance, the routine was Mr. Osborne taking all the children, BTK would have seen the children and Mr.Osborne get in and leave.  If he wasn’t counting, he might think they were following their routine and all five children were gone. <BR>He doesn’t think anyone is there but Mrs. Osborne until he pushes his way in. <BR> <BR> <BR>1.  Why didn&#39;t he wait for the other children to come home?  Because two children had gone to school, and lunchtime becomes a problem because: <BR> <BR>     a.  Photos show considerable snow, if the children at school are expecting to come home for lunch, and there&#39;s no ride, they call and there&#39;s no answer &#40;I don&#39;t know what it sounds like to call a phone that’s been cut&#41; but someone at school could report trouble on the line and repairmen show up.  A child at school with a missing ride can be an issue.   <BR> <BR>     b.  BTK could not be sure the children wouldn&#39;t get a ride home at noon from a teacher or another parent, or that they wouldn&#39;t come home with a friend for lunch.  Same for after school. <BR> <BR>     c. One or all three might stay after school, or go to a friend’s house, etc. <BR> <BR>This could explain why he didn&#39;t wait for the remaining children: it&#39;s too unpredictable in terms of how long he waits, what if they get a ride from a concerned teacher who waits in a their car in the driveway for an &#34;OK&#34;.  <BR> <BR>[This would also set a time frame on the killing: he had to be done long enough before noon that he&#39;s gone before there&#39;s any risk of the children coming home for lunch.  This fits the reported time of death as “sometime before noon” ”<a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/history/8312877.htm" target=_top>http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_pack ages/btk/history/8312877.htm</a>] <BR> <BR>2.  Why didn&#39;t the surviving children identify BTK, or put another way, if the two children in the house knew who BTK was why didn&#39;t the surviving children know also? <BR> <BR>     a.  All the children may have known who he was, but only the two at home have the specialized knowledge that he is the killer. <BR> <BR>     b.  The two children who went to school lack this specialized knowledge.  They might have known him, but not being there they could not link him to the killing of their parents.  At best they could only identify him as one of hundreds of people their parents knew.  This explains why the two at home are killed as witnesses, even though their siblings couldn&#39;t identify the killer <BR> <BR>     c.  Immediately afterwards the children were taken into protective custody by SRS &#40;a child welfare agency&#41; and ultimately placed with family friends in New Mexico.  He couldn&#39;t find them. <BR> <BR>     d.  Also it would have soon been obvious to BTK that neither surviving child had given the police a &#34;smoking gun&#34; suspect, and the need to pursue them would diminish. <BR> <BR>     e.  If the secret relationship between BTK and Mr. Osborne were so awful that he couldn&#39;t tell police, it wouldn&#39;t be unusual for a father to have concealed this kind of secret from his children. <BR> <BR> <BR>Skoal and J <BR> <BR>Thanks for the questions and critique [I tend to fall in love with my own theories; reality checks are always welcome] <BR> <BR>Good points on the MO.  Is it possible, though, that BTK may have combined business and pleasure; in other words, if he was going to kill anyway enjoying the act is a bonus. <BR> <BR>Or, he may have learned to like it in this event, he may have been unaware of his tendencies until this killing, Mike_Kelleher could speak to that better. <BR> <BR>Again please don’t get hung up on the drug issue, there’s no evidence of &#42;any&#42; criminal activity by any Otero.  All I’m saying is that Charlie Otero’s statement raises two &#42; red flags&#42;: 1&#41; why did BTK want to hurt the Otero’s, and 2&#41; knowing of the threat why didn’t Mr. Otero call police? <BR> <BR> <BR>I&#39;m proposing this hypothesis to test the assumption that C.O. was accurately reporting his father&#39;s awareness of a serious threat to his family rather than dismissing it out-of-hand because it doesn&#39;t fit a given theory of profile.  Any plausible theory/profile must account for &#42;all&#42; of the evidence, not just some of it. <BR> <BR>I remain concerned about a procrustean analytical process that rejects facts and evidence because they don&#39;t fit someone&#39;s theory,  “Procruste’s Bed” &#40;<a href="http://www.bartleby.com/81/13673.html" target=_top>http://www.bartleby.com/81/13673.html</a>&#41;. <BR> <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3287-->
<!--Post: 3289--><!--Time: 1104741242-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3289"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Q<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Q<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 12:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Whoisbtk, <BR> <BR>You wrote: &#34;I&#39;m proposing this hypothesis to test the assumption that C.O. was accurately reporting his father&#39;s awareness of a serious threat to his family&#34; <BR> <BR>If this is the case, as C.O. asserted &#40;when did he say this...back in the 70&#39;s or more recent?&#41; then why would Mr. Otero leave his two children and wife alone? <BR> <BR>1. He thought the trip to be a short one and in daytime? <BR> <BR>2. I read that the family were all Judo students but then why hide them in a closet? <BR> <BR>3. He thought the threat had passed or wouldn&#39;t or couldn&#39;t happen at that time of day, day of the week? <BR> <BR>4. He was mislead to believe the threat had passed or wouldn&#39;t happen purposly by BTK because they had a close relashionship of some kind either including his wife or not... professional? <BR> <BR> Something else?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3289-->
<!--Post: 3306--><!--Time: 1104774302-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3306"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 9:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dr. Kelleher- <BR> <BR>I hope to see your comments regarding Zodiac and BTK one day soon.  As a reader of <i>This is the Zodiac Speaking</i>, I understand you to believe the murderer of Cheri Jo Bates to _not_ be the Zodiac, but someone known to the Zodiac &#40;a boyhood friend, perhaps&#41;.  Is this correct?  A very farfetched theory discussed on this message board involved a &#34;suspect&#34; who originated from the general Riverside, CA area, and it reminded me of this theory of yours....  I believe Tom has expunged references to this &#34;suspect&#34; from the board. <BR> <BR>I think it&#39;s glaring to those familiar with both cases that BTK has not only a fascination with the Zodiac, but seems to want to link himself to the Zodiac in some way; to intertwine their crimes by &#34;copying&#34; language from letters, details of crimes, etc..  I hope in your comments regarding BTK and Zodiac you might include some insight into this.  Why does BTK seem to have a fascination with the Zodiac?  Why the Zodiac in particular &#40;instead of Bundy, or Gein, for examples&#41;? Why does BTK feel compelled to muddy his crimes with the crimes of the Zodiac?  What conclusions can be drawn about BTK&#39;s underlying psychology from these facts, and what clues as to BTK&#39;s daily life might these facts provide &#40;for instance, you have said that we should expect BTK to be monitoring and participating in internet discussion of his own case- might we also expect him to be interacting at _Zodiac_ crime websites or with other Zodiac crime buffs via the internet?&#41;?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3306-->
<!--Post: 3307--><!--Time: 1104775331-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3307"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 10:02 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Dr. Kelleher- <BR> <BR>P.S. On a reread of my post, I realize I might have been too obtuse in my first thought: I wonder if you suspect BTK might have more than a &#34;purely intellectual/psychological&#34; connection to the Zodiac.  For example, would your investigative BTK profile include to look for a suspect&#39;s connection during the 1960&#39;s or 70&#39;s to Vallejo, San Francisco, Napa, or Riverside, CA?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3307-->
<!--Post: 3308--><!--Time: 1104775704-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3308"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Mike_kelleher<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mike_kelleher<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 10:08 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m not sure about the BTK/Zodiac connection. BTK does show an &#34;interest&#34; in Zodiac methodology but it&#39;s hard to say if there is any more to it. Zodiac was a very unique killer and an obvious master of manipulating the media. From that point of view, others may want to emulate his behavior and get the attention he got. If there&#39;s more to it than this aspect, I haven&#39;t seen any proof.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3308-->
<!--Post: 3322--><!--Time: 1104800087-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3322"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Armchairpi<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Armchairpi<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 03, 2005 - 4:54 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m guessing you believe the writing to the police and press, the phone calls, and the selection/announcement of a scary moniker and symbol fall into the category of &#34;showing an interest in Zodiac methodology&#34;. <BR> <BR>But, I&#39;m also referring to some other items that have been discussed in a couple or three well marked threads regarding BTK &amp; Zodiac.  Ones that come to mind are: <BR> <BR>1&#41;leaving behind a single clear print at one of the crime scenes while at the same time seeming to be so meticulous in general not to leave prints &#40;some speculate this is an homage to the Zodiac-Stine cab prints&#41;; <BR> <BR>2&#41; at least one turn of a Zodiac phrase &#40;&#34;Will there be more?&#34;&#41; in police-corrborated BTK correspondence, and other phrases from poster&#40;s&#41; on the message board suspected by some to be BTK; <BR> <BR>3&#41; a possible &#34;Riverside&#34;/&#34;Indian Hills&#34; correlation between Cheri Jo Bates and Vicki Wegerle &#40;if I understand correctly, V.W. is the only major suspected BTK victim to be outside of an otherwise tight radius and lived in &#34;Indian Hills&#34;, which is extremely close to an area of Wichita known as &#34;Riverside&#34;; while CJB lived in Riverside, which has an &#34;Indian Hills&#34; very nearby it&#41;; <BR> <BR>4&#41; as Tom pointed out, a striking similarity in the way the Bright attack was committed in comparison to Berryessa &#40;I might add to what Tom said that, if I&#39;m not mistaken, in both attacks the woman died, while the man survived, &#42;and&#42; in both the perp made idle chit chat: &#34;escaped from Montana penitentiary&#34; and &#34;haven&#39;t I seen you at the university?&#34;&#41;; <BR> <BR>5&#41; a plea by BTK for more press coverage &#40;much like Z&#39;s demands for column inches and Zodiac buttons, etc.&#41;, while oddly leaving the Zodiac &#42;out&#42; of a long list of serial killers who got a lot of press; <BR> <BR>6&#41; many correlations between Zodiac/BTK dates and numerology. <BR> <BR>You&#39;re right- not &#34;proof&#34;, but do you think these coincidences are suspicious and might have implications on a BTK profile?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3322-->
<!--Post: 3365--><!--Time: 1104826345-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3365"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Oklahoma_mike<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->11-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 12:12 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->See my upcoming post regarding some of these issues in the Victims-Oteros thread.  We get a bit far afield here at times,<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3365-->
<!--Post: 3385--><!--Time: 1104860418-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3385"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 9:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Q <BR>Good questions <BR> <BR>1. Charlie Otero said this in a phone interview with an AP reporter, Roxana Hegeman, either 11/30/2004 or 12/1/2004.  The story ran in the Dodge City Daily Globe on December 1, 2004 &#40;<a href="http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_120104008.shtml" target=_top>http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_1201040 08.shtml</a>&#41; <BR>  <BR>My vote for most likely is #1, a short trip in daylight. Here are the route, distances, and times: <BR> <BR>Edgemoor to 2nd street &#40;1/2mi.&#41; to Oliver &#40;1/2mi.&#41;, drop the children off on the school side of Oliver. Then Oliver to Central &#40;1/4mi.&#41; to Edgemoor &#40;1/2mi.&#41;To 803 Edgemoor &#40;1/4mi.&#41; The distance is 2 miles with 4 traffic lights and one 20mph school zone.  Even on icy roads, getting stuck at all the signals and stopped in the school zone, a 20mph average makes a 6min. trip.  Add 5 min. for signals and school zones; it&#39;s a 10-12 min. trip.  [Mapquest has the round trip as 1.96 miles, 6 min. drive time] <BR> <BR>Bottom line, it&#39;s about a 10 min trip. <BR> <BR>So it&#39;s short, in daylight, and the alternative is have the children get to school themselves, but: <BR> <BR>a.  Wichita Public Schools will not bus students who live within 2 miles of school.  The Otero home was one mile from school and had no school bus, they would have walked, which is more dangerous for them if BTK is stalking the family. <BR> <BR>b. Even if danger to the children isn&#39;t a factor, the weather was probably too bad for walking a mile.  Photos of the Otero home taken later in the day show snow on the east side of the home and slush in the street.  The neighbor that called police was shoveling snow when the children came home from school.  This indicates cold weather and recent snowfall.  Living in Wichita I am aware that it would have been cold, windy, and icy that morning.  The children needed a ride because of the weather seems like the best explanation.   <BR> <BR>So, &#34; He thought the trip to be a short one and in daytime&#34; with the added factor of weather on a walk to school seems likely. <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3385-->
<!--Post: 3388--><!--Time: 1104861406-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3388"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 9:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Whoisbtk <BR> <BR>Here is what I found about the weather jan 15th 1974. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.google.dk/search?q=cache:9H9A3cYrd98J:www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk/archive/8348962.htm%2Bbtk%2B%2Bsun%2B%2Botero%2B%2Bsnow&amp;hl=en" target=_top>http://www.google.dk/search?q=cache:9H9A3cYrd98J:w ww.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/special_packages/btk /archive/8348962.htm&#43;btk&#43;%2Bsun&#43;%2Botero&#43;%2Bsnow&amp;h l=en</a> <BR> <BR>In northeast Wichita, the sun was turning snow to slush when Charlie Otero returned home from Robinson Junior High School at 3:40 p.m.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3388-->
<!--Post: 3437--><!--Time: 1104896029-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3437"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 7:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Mike_kelleher <BR> <BR>Could we address the &#34;memory filling&#34; issue again, please? <BR> <BR>After the WPD release of details on 11/30/2004, Charlie Otero had a phone interview with an AP reporter from Dodge City, published 12/1/2004. [Link: <a href="http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_1201040" target=_top>http://dodgeglobe.com/stories/120104/state_1201040</a> 08.shtml]  In this interview, he says he thought his father knew BTK.  In support, he recounts three specific events: <BR> <BR>1. Power went out in the house.  Mr. Otero made the family get in a closet and stay until he learned that power was out in the neighborhood. <BR> <BR>2.  A telephone repairman came to the house.  Mr. Otero wouldn&#39;t let him in until he saw a phone company truck. <BR> <BR>3.  Shortly before the murders, Mr. Otero tried to give Charlie his ring in case something should happen to him.  Charlie says he told his father that he &#40;the father&#41; would probably outlive him &#40;Charlie&#41;. <BR> <BR>Are these three specific recollections typical of &#34;memory filling&#34;? <BR> <BR>As a followup, if appropriate to this thread, why would Mr. Otero not call the police? <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3437-->
